# python.env — OPTIONAL — where MyGPT's launcher scripts find Python.
#
# run.sh (Linux/macOS), run.bat (Windows), updater.sh and updater.bat
# resolve the interpreter in this order (first valid one wins):
#   1. this file, if present  ->  PYTHON=<path>
#   2. the 2PY2 environment variable ("second python" — for portable /
#      embeddable Python users; the name means a *second* python, not python2)
#   3. the project .venv, then python3 / python on PATH
#
# Set PYTHON to an absolute path, or a path relative to this folder. If this
# file is deleted the scripts simply use 2PY2 / the venv fallbacks.
# The interpreter must have MyGPT's dependencies installed
# (pip install -r requirements.txt).
#
# Examples:
#   PYTHON=.venv/bin/python              Linux/macOS project venv (default)
#   PYTHON=.venv\Scripts\python.exe      Windows project venv
#   PYTHON=/usr/bin/python3              system interpreter
#   PYTHON=C:\Python312\python.exe       Windows absolute path
PYTHON=.venv/bin/python
